{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed","id":833620,"title":"Harvesting Glamour in 2ED","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-19T18:10:10-08:00","id":833620,"title":"Harvesting Glamour in 2ED","content":"So I thought that this subtopic is locking a bit normal discussion on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks\">Playtests Files</a> in's and out's, but is one of fundamental for the 2ED Playtests on itself. To say that I have strong disappointment in Harvesting Emotions in 1ED <b>Changeling</b> is a bit understatement. This is why I was so please to read something very similar to my own thoughts made by <b>Axelgear</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833536#post833536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Reticent is that it doesn't do what you're asking, Arcane. The consequences of fanning people's emotions should be the natural consequences of fanning people's emotions. You don't need a supernatural consequence to make that hurt more. If anything, Reticent's emotional draining <i>hurts</i> that angle: Instead of exemplifying emotion's power to take you on a rollercoaster of psychic torment, it leaves you internally dead. It negates, instead of exemplifying.<br /> <br /> The solution should be to give Changelings <i>more</i> reason to play with people's emotions, and then let them deal with the natural fall-out. not to have feeding itself be harmful. The muse who drives her artist lover to mad excess should see what it does to him; see how he forgets personal hygeine and sleep in favour of sitting at his easel for days on end; how he stops leaving his studio except to see her; how he stands outside her house at night, crying for her to come to him because he cannot think of anything but her. When he finally hangs himself because she can't deal with this and spurns him, she should feel the horror of the act as if she tied the rope herself.<br /> <br /> <i>That</i> should be the consequence for playing with people's emotions and treating human beings like they're batteries; the natural consequences of strong emotions. Emotions with all the force of a hurricane, and all the devastation of a forest fire. The high drama and low melancholy of a Byron play.<br /> <br /> At present, though, Changelings have no need or reason to produce that sort of feeling. A Changeling can just hang out in a club all night and feed to their heart's content, and never devastate any lives in their passing. Reticent not only doesn't change that to what you're after, it actively makes it <i>worse</i> by taking away the very capacity to toy with emotions that so often fills these stories and that you, yourself, are trying to create.<br /> <br /> Reticent may be softer than what you'd have done, but I hope that what you'd have done would actually encourage strong and powerful emotions to drive the drama, rather than deaden them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Myself, I would go with making victims of Emotional Harvesting to get Addicted to the catharsis of it. They <b>both</b> lost 1 Willpower per Glamour sucked ( and are a bit emotional dead by it ), but on the other hand they want to relive those intense emotions that changeling is brought to them - and get Addicted Condition on sucked Emotion. Victims felt real, pure emotion on Harvesting, but also feel they lost it now - and want to reclaim it. Or at least when they get back Willpower of their.<br /> <br /> <i>This</i> will lead to mad poets going to their muse in the middle of the night. To people actively looking for the real scare only Autumn Court can provide. But it also makes changelings true psychic vampires, sucking Willpower of their victim, entwining them like Kindred do with their Kiss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-19-2016, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:11:41-08:00","id":833698,"title":"","content":"Y'know, maybe it's that Arthurian Lit course talking, but historically speaking the intimate attentions of visiting fae in media have produced much fewer thrill-seekers than burnouts.<br /> <br /> The resolution criteria could definitely stand to be less dauntingly phrased for what they are, but it's already set up such that the average Reticent subject who doesn't simply run out the clock gets their groove back by being inspired or actualized into having a fulfilling experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:22:09-08:00","id":833703,"title":"","content":"One possible compromise would be a Merit that allows you to feed relatively &quot;safely,&quot; at least to a point\u2014feeding drains Willpower, and if you go too far, you'll still cause Reticent on the target. Maybe something along those lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:25:43-08:00","id":833706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=833698#post833698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, maybe it's that Arthurian Lit course talking, but historically speaking the intimate attentions of visiting fae in media have produced much fewer thrill-seekers than burnouts.<br /> <br /> The resolution criteria could definitely stand to be less dauntingly phrased for what they are, but it's already set up such that the average Reticent subject who doesn't simply run out the clock gets their groove back by being inspired or actualized into having a fulfilling experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, that angle kinda falls flat a bit when the condition only gives beats when resolved (and even then, just one). I could see the self-actualisation angle if it gave beats when learning to rediscover emotion.<br /> <br /> But then it might cause Changelings to rationalise their actions as positive in the end, when perhaps they shouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:35:24-08:00","id":833708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=833706#post833706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, that angle kinda falls flat a bit when the condition only gives beats when resolved (and even then, just one). I could see the self-actualisation angle if it gave beats when learning to rediscover emotion.<br /> <br /> But then it might cause Changelings to rationalise their actions as positive in the end, when perhaps they shouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no &quot;angle.&quot; I'm saying that if you don't simply get out of the funk with time it's because you've been moved by the activity of yourself or another or serendipity despite the emotional inertia that the Condition entails. That's pretty much as close to a straightforward statement of fact as you can get from an outside look at narrative mechanics that are subject to change. Whether or not a given changeling goes out of their way to facilitate a reboot of their dinner date's sentimentality out of a sense of practicality or responsibility is kind of outside the scope of that assessment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T21:39:43-08:00","id":833710,"title":"","content":"<b>I'm not sure I like even idea of <i>Reticent Condition</i></b> - I support losing Willpower, but truly &quot;deading&quot; of emotions of character is a unnecessarily. <b><i>Low Willpower</i></b> means that character is in bad psychic state and a bit &quot;dull&quot;, de-invigorated, so to speak. Also, low Willpower means that your character - at it is - much less prepared for the life struggles. And not even we go to combat area in there where each Willpower spent can be win-or-lose situation...<br /> <br /> <i>Points</i> losing Willpower for victim would be enough for make Emotional Harvesting a &quot;bad thing&quot; for the victim. Question is - <b>Should it be all? I would rather want the mortals to be compelled to go over and become more and more obsessed with changeling. </b>The other way it will end like in Vampire - <i>&quot;Today I bite this Random Chick Nr 5 in bar&quot;</i> instead of <i>&quot;I prepare complex scare scene to feed on the Fear of this unsuspecting teenagers that come again and again on my junkyard&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>I could see <i>Reticent Condition </i>as Dramatic Failure effect, where instead of getting Glamour and making &quot;healthy&quot; connection to Harvesting victim - changeling is blocking her, making big flare of emotions in one swipe.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T22:17:51-08:00","id":833717,"title":"","content":"There are two main aspects to the Reticent thing, as I see it. One, as mentioned in the other thread, is that, if nothing else, it has matched my experience with the sort listlessness and depression that can (and often does) come after an emotional high...which admittedly isn't always in play with harvesting. The other is that it keeps players from locking into just one easy source of Glamour, emotionally speaking, thus encouraging more varied stories when it comes to harvesting.<br /> <br /> I can sort of see some of the dissatisfaction with that, but my feelings on that aren't a secret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T23:05:35-08:00","id":833722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=833717#post833717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One, as mentioned in the other thread, is that, if nothing else, it has matched my experience with the sort listlessness and depression that can (and often does) come after an emotional high....</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue I see with this is that, the Lost isn't the one who becomes depressed and apathetic. The lost is Forcing others to be depressed and apathetic, and I haven't seen any experience of that in real life with people who have gone through trauma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T23:15:42-08:00","id":833725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=833722#post833722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue I see with this is that, the Lost isn't the one who becomes depressed and apathetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lost is also not the one experiencing an emotional high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T23:16:34-08:00","id":833727,"title":"","content":"THis is where that blurring between metaphor and narrative occur. But putting that aside for now, of course the Lost aren't dealing with the emotional 'power outage'. They make other people experience a high, devour it, and that makes the person go low.<br /> <br /> There's some blurring here between how far do we take the metaphor, because Changeling is not a one to one metaphor for trauma survival, even with that as its' theme. But if you wanted to argue about that on theme, it <i>does</i> tie into one of the common problems for people recovering-people getting burnt out on their problems. It happens, empathy can have it's limits, and for people recovering, it's easy to find those limits in pursuit of something to fill the hole in their hearts.<br /> <br /> Not a perfect metaphor, and I'm disinclined to use it in favor of the simpler fact that in deciding that changelings harvest emotions, one must consider the very simplest emotional outcomes of highs. It's simply writ large given the fact we're dealing with fae rather than normal circumstances.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I get why that might be unsatisfactory with some. I don't share it though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T23:46:26-08:00","id":833733,"title":"","content":"Or you could just have it be &quot;It works the way the &quot;fluff&quot; says it does and it isn't predatory at all&quot;. Why have them be predatory? Thematically I mean. It seems rather out of nowhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T23:53:21-08:00","id":833735,"title":"","content":"Them not being predatory felt out of place for me, so this is one them there impasses I hear tell about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T00:01:10-08:00","id":833737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=833733#post833733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could just have it be &quot;It works the way the &quot;fluff&quot; says it does and it isn't predatory at all&quot;. Why have them be predatory? Thematically I mean. It seems rather out of nowhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having there be a hard line between the Good Folk and the elves that took Tam Lin solely chalked up to &quot;well obviously the good ones were changelings and the bad ones were True Fae&quot; was not an aspect of 1e that followed logically from &quot;you escaped from a place where your sense of right and wrong (and reality besides) was put through a blender, you may or may not have developed a taste for cannibalism, and you have a better handle on what happened in your dreams last week than what your brother-in-arms wore to the celebratory banquet in his honor last night.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Kindly Ones and their errant subjects do not <i>do</i> clear-cut outside the context of a work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T00:15:11-08:00","id":833740,"title":"","content":"It needn't be an impasse. A Merit could solve this problem by including the middle ground. We'll see what David says, but I am sure we can figure out how to make it work\u2014and this is one of the beauties of open development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T00:18:45-08:00","id":833741,"title":"","content":"I might argue that there is one about the subject of whether Changelings should have a certain amount of predatory element inherently baked into them or not. And a Merit feels like a tax to avoid a certain element of the game, which last I checked was not quite the purpose of Merits. Hacks, maybe, but not Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T00:51:27-08:00","id":833746,"title":"","content":"Merits are there to help define abilities, knowledges, and other traits not represented by Attributes and Skills. We have a Merit that allows you to reap Glamour from supernatural creatures and gain new benefits with it, so one that shows how you are a more refined connoisseur of emotion that doesn't need to drain targets dry of their energy is pretty much exactly what Merits are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T01:03:24-08:00","id":833749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/831430-changeling-playtestable-chunks?p=833734#post833734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am having serious trouble believing no one here has had the experience of having an emotional high followed by a couple of days on an emotional low. Like, I am fairly sure this is an actual, regular, common thing, so my only course of belief here is that people here aren't experiencing emotional highs, and that sounds <i>insane</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had episodes of <i>hours</i> of this kind burnout, maybe a day max. I heard about it from my psych buddies, but it's very individual thing. That's why I would rather left <b><i>Reticent Condition as Dramatic Failure </i></b>thing and do the Willpower sapping on this &quot;dead inside&quot; to represent it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T01:14:44-08:00","id":833750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=833746#post833746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merits are there to help define abilities, knowledges, and other traits not represented by Attributes and Skills. We have a Merit that allows you to reap Glamour from supernatural creatures and gain new benefits with it, so one that shows how you are a more refined connoisseur of emotion that doesn't need to drain targets dry of their energy is pretty much exactly what Merits are for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But those two things aren't really comparable -- Vampire has a merit that allows you to feed off of Ghosts, but that's hardly justification for a merit that decreases the damage you do when you feed off of people.<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't mind a merit addressing this. THAT said, such a merit should have some non-mild drawbacks -- spending a willpower to do a &quot;light drain&quot;, get half your successes in Glamour, and cause a much more mild condition is the sort of thing I'd expect/hope for if such a merit comes to pass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T01:21:41-08:00","id":833752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=833750#post833750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But those two things aren't really comparable -- Vampire has a merit that allows you to feed off of Ghosts, but that's hardly justification for a merit that decreases the damage you do when you feed off of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the differences are more pronounced there. Vampires are literally biting and drinking the blood of their targets. There's not really any way to minimize that, compared to a changeling learning not to suck up all of a person's emotional energy. I mean, it's more feasible for a changeling to learn some way to minimize their impact compared to actually physically removing the blood in a person's body.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T01:51:37-08:00","id":833756,"title":"","content":"I don't have the time to check out the rules right now, but I was wondering if there's a middle ground where you can kinda sip safely and guzzle in a predatory manner?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T02:34:01-08:00","id":833762,"title":"","content":"Does harvesting from dreams cause Reticient? Because if not there's a safe means of feeding right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T04:49:43-08:00","id":833780,"title":"","content":"What about harvesting glamour from emotions that you didn't cause? My big problem with reticent is that it draws no distinction between the Autumn Courtier at a horror film and the one using Paralyzing Shudder in a back alley. The people at the horror film expect to be scared, presumably *want* to be scared, and it feels really out of place to stick them with such a draining condition regardless of circumstance.<br /> <br /> I think Reticent makes sense as a possible consequence of glamour harvesting, but having it be automatic and unavoidable actually works against persuading people to feed carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T06:38:50-08:00","id":833805,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I really feel that if you go out of your way to find or engineer a situation where many mortals are experiencing the same emotion fairly strongly, you should be able to harvest safely, even if it takes you a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T06:54:46-08:00","id":833810,"title":"","content":"Who would even get the condition if you sucked up a cinema full of horror fans, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T07:53:22-08:00","id":833830,"title":"","content":"Like I said before, make it a dramatic failure, and tone it down abit. So its always a risk, but not asure thing that it happens. Just my 2 cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T07:55:31-08:00","id":833833,"title":"","content":"I don't understand the problem. Feeding on emotions is a bad thing for the victim in pretty much any lore or story or myth. And its generally something that results in apathy.<br /> <br /> It seems like people are asking for an upswing in other emotions? I don't really understand the issue here. Are people not happy with changelings being monsters and needing to go all predatorial now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-20-2016, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T08:09:31-08:00","id":833842,"title":"","content":"I think there are a few issues here (this is just for clarification for anybody who doesn't understand what's being argued):<br /> <br /> 1) Some people don't agree that emotional feeding should have a consequence. 1e explained how it's possible to simply sup on the &quot;emotional effluents&quot; of a person and not on their &quot;emotional core&quot;. Under this view, Changelings would be like cold people simply basking in the warmth of a fire (which does not actually diminish the fire at all).<br /> 2) Some people agree that emotional feeding should have a consequence, but they don't agree Reticent is the right one. Some would rather see different Conditions or effects.<br /> 3) Some people agree on something like Reticent being an acceptable consequence for emotional feeding, but find the Condition far too mechanically harsh, or too easily inflicted.<br /> 4) Some people would like more nuance and granularity in emotional feeding, so that changelings have more options and it isn't an all-or-nothing affair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T08:10:37-08:00","id":833844,"title":"","content":"What I'm asking for, at least, is for there to be a gradient of consequences. As it stands right now there's no difference between harvesting 1 glamour or 10, the victim loses all willpower either way. There's no mechanical difference between a light, cautious feeding and going for broke. It doesn't matter how much you mess with their emotions before feeding or how heavily you feed, it all ends in the same state of numb indifference. And that's contrary to narratives about being cautious with how you go about it, caution is rendered meaningless, irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T09:17:16-08:00","id":833869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=833833#post833833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the problem. Feeding on emotions is a bad thing for the victim in pretty much any lore or story or myth. And its generally something that results in apathy.<br /> <br /> It seems like people are asking for an upswing in other emotions? I don't really understand the issue here. Are people not happy with changelings being monsters and needing to go all predatorial now?</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the part of changelings being predators now, but I think that I'm not speaking for the majority.<br /> My players haven't liked this and I can understand why. On the 1ed they were a bunch of misunderstood people who having being taken by the Fae and escaped back and haven found themselfs needing to feed from other peoples emotions, but that action didn't bring much risk for the donator. They liked to seem themselfs as the good guys, in a symbiotic way. Thay feed from human emotions, but that didn't cause any harm or trouble. Heck... they try to get rid of the local vampires for sucking some people blood(and life). <br /> <br /> Now, in the 2ed, they were asking me: &quot;What differs me from a bloodsucking vampire?&quot; and &quot;Can we ignore this Condition?&quot;.<br /> <br /> My thought about this is simple: &quot;I loved it&quot;. But I'm not using the Condition, because my players want to maintain the old Mood of emotion feeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 02-20-2016, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T09:27:07-08:00","id":833875,"title":"","content":"You really can't argue that what changelings do now isn't vampirism, because we know that in Hurt Locker there's going to be something that can do exactly the same thing <i>called </i>&quot;Psychic Vampires&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T09:36:26-08:00","id":833880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=833875#post833875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really can't argue that what changelings do now isn't vampirism, because we know that in Hurt Locker there's going to be something that can do exactly the same thing <i>called </i>&quot;Psychic Vampires&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who don't inflict the Reticent or Drained condition on people, merely leaving them either damaged, Willpower-deprived, or both.<br /> <br /> Of course, they're not fully supernatural, but they can pick up a Supernatural Resistance merit and a bag of nifty tricks. And since minor templates stack, they can also be Fae-Touched, Ghouls and so on. So, you know. Close enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T10:09:27-08:00","id":833897,"title":"","content":"Veddy eenterestink.<br /> <br /> There are excellent points on all sides. Yes, people who get emotional highs tend to get &quot;drops&quot; a bit later, which makes them listless and depressed. The Reticent condition does a fair job of reflecting that, though it does seem a little harsh.<br /> <br /> To carry the comparison with vampires to its logical conclusion, especially as regards some kind of &quot;light feeding&quot; Merit and such a Merit being a tax to bypass rules: Vampire can inflict, say, three Conditions on people they feed from: None At All (taking only a little blood), Wound Penalties (taking blood into their last three health boxes), or Dead (taking it all.) This is intrinsic to how they feed, and any of them can be done by any Vampire, anywhere, at any time (barring daytime, because daytime.) Changelings, as the draft stands, can only ever induce the Reticent Condition, no matter how lightly or deeply they feed, which I agree seems wrong. If a neonate Vampire, straight out of the box, can control their feeding with such precision, why can't a Changeling? More to the point, does a Vampire's ability to take one Vitae from seven people instead of seven Vitae from one person (thus, on average, killing them) make them any less predatory? In the same, uh, vein (sorry about that) would a Changeling being able to take emotional energy from a dozen people, leaving them mostly unharmed, instead of draining all the emotional capability from one person make them any less predatory?<br /> <br /> To again carry the Vampire analogy, Vampires can choose not to prey on humans, subsisting on animals, but this is really only effective for very young vampires, and doesn't satisfy the way human blood does. Similarly, Changelings should be able to choose not to &quot;prey&quot; on humans, instead harmlessly absorbing the ambient emotion of people surrounding them, but this should really only be effective for Changelings with very low Wyrd. In the same way that animal blood just isn't efficient enough to keep vampires sustained for very long (and won't do at all past Blood Potency 2), gathering up whatever stray emotional energy is available randomly shouldn't be efficient enough to keep a Changeling sustained for very long, and probably shouldn't suffice at all past a certain level of Wyrd. Think about again like a blood analogy. It is far more efficient for a vampire to poke holes in her victim with her teeth and have the blood flow straight into her mouth than it would be to slice her victim's throat, open her mouth, and be content with however much of the fountain happened to land on her tongue. To obtain the focused, directed burst of emotion that a Changeling can claim as theirs, and only theirs, and feed from efficiently, something more must be done.<br /> <br /> This, to me, is where the discussion about toying with someone's emotions becomes really fucking interesting. Changelings who cultivate herds to feed from need to engender the kinds of emotion they want, and this can have serious long-term effects, and may even result in diminishing returns (keeping someone in a perpetual state of joy, lust, anxiety, or fear will eventually deaden them to those emotions, as their brain and body adapt to this being the new &quot;normal.&quot;) Changelings who feed from different random strangers every night are elements of chaos, sweeping into their victims' lives by chance, having a momentary but unforgettable effect, then vanishing, never to be seen again. Both are sterling examples of bringing the bad parts of Arcadia back with you.<br /> <br /> Changelings should be able to be careful when feeding, but they still need to manipulate victims into feeling enough emotion that they can glean sustenance from. This is not going to be perfectly harmless for their victims, but steps should be able to be taken to minimize that harm, in the same way a Vampire can choose to minimize the harm they do by feeding from a mortal's blood. In my opinion, the Reticient Condition should be the Changeling equivalent of a Vampire draining a mortal dry, either something a newbie Changeling has done because they fucked up and (hopefully) learned a hard lesson from, or something sadistic Changelings do just because they enjoy it. And part of the sadistic choice of Vampire/Changeling existence: &quot;I need Vitae/Glamour badly, do I grab the first person I see and take everything that they have, or do I try and be careful and cautious and risk not having enough when the bigger Vampire/Privateer finally catches up with me? And I'm <i>just so <b>fucking <u>HUNGRY</u></b>.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> There really should be some kind of gradiation to Changeling feeding. Anything else, I feel, cheapens the horror of those times, even with the best of intentions, a character is just too hungry not to clean their plate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T10:18:04-08:00","id":833904,"title":"","content":"Vampires inflict the Drained condition if they drain more Vitae than the victim's Stamina. Perhaps the same could be done for Reticent and the person's Composure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T10:19:15-08:00","id":833905,"title":"","content":"Vampires inflict the Drained condition when they feed too much from a target when they feed more than the target Stamina dots. But they can try to not do that.<br /> For the Reticent condition, I'm planning to use it(After I talk to my players about that) but im a simmilar way to the drained condition.<br /> You only get Reticent if you have been harvest more than your Composure dots. The thing is: I didn't saw anywhere that changelings(low wyrd ones at least) need Glamour to wake up and live.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your character has been fed from extensively, and suffers from<br /> blood loss. He suffers a \u20132 die penalty to any physical actions,<br /> and rolls to stabilize and survive injuries. As well, after any scene<br /> where he exerts himself physically, he must make a Stamina roll<br /> or fall unconscious for an hour or more. The Drained penalty<br /> does not apply to the Stamina roll, but any wound penalties do<br /> apply. Taking damage, being fed from, or spending Willpower<br /> on a physical roll applies as physical exertion for this Condition.<br /> Possible Sources: A vampire\u2019s feeding.<br /> Resolution: All lethal damage healed through normal means.<br /> Beat: n/a </div> </div> </div>Edit: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10056\" data-vbnamecard=\"10056\">ShadowKnight1224</a> already gave the suggestion. lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 02-20-2016, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T11:39:25-08:00","id":833936,"title":"","content":"Eh, forgot about the Drained Condition. My ChroD game is on indefinite hiatus, so I'm not fresh on the rules (and only have Requiem 2E anyway.)<br /> <br /> I'd almost say a lesser Condition for taking more Glamour than a mortal's Composure, and Reticent for taking ALL THE GLAMOUR. Or a worse Condition for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":831,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","user":"ErikModi","date":". 02-20-2016, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T12:57:02-08:00","id":833983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=833905#post833905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires inflict the Drained condition when they feed too much from a target when they feed more than the target Stamina dots. But they can try to not do that.<br /> For the Reticent condition, I'm planning to use it(After I talk to my players about that) but im a simmilar way to the drained condition.<br /> You only get Reticent if you have been harvest more than your Composure dots. The thing is: I didn't saw anywhere that changelings(low wyrd ones at least) need Glamour to wake up and live.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> already gave the suggestion. lol</div> </div> </div> </div> Love, love, love this idea. The being said it makes the Dearhearts alittle scarier, because they drop composure with a touch, which is cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T13:32:49-08:00","id":833999,"title":"","content":"The feeding rules for Vampires are a little different too. With a succesful roll, you find a victim in 1 hour, you decide how much you will drain and etc. But changelings get Glamour per success and I think that they can harvest from various sources at the same time(movie room, etc), I'm not sure how I'm going to balance it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T13:38:16-08:00","id":834008,"title":"","content":"You'd probably need them to be able to take glamour <i>up to</i> their successes or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T18:24:24-08:00","id":834172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=833905#post833905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is: I didn't saw anywhere that changelings(low wyrd ones at least) need Glamour to wake up and live.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd addiction rules make it so all changelings need glamour or they don't gain any sustenance from food or water and starve to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T19:59:12-08:00","id":834206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=834172#post834172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd addiction rules make it so all changelings need glamour or they don't gain any sustenance from food or water and starve to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the level where their metaphysical framework can support a superhuman baseline of traits.<br /> <br /> Which is dependent upon an electively increased rating that can also be reduced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T20:46:11-08:00","id":834233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/833620-harvesting-glamour-in-2ed?p=834206#post834206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the level where their metaphysical framework can support a superhuman baseline of traits.<br /> <br /> Which is dependent upon an electively increased rating that can also be reduced.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the glamour addicition section says it only applies to 6 wyrd+ changelings, there is a section of Glamour Addiction that applies to all changelings (admittedly, it could be better formatted).<br /> <br /> Here (bolded for emphasis):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, a changeling at 0 Glamour begins to suffer from both physical deprivation, as though starving, as well as suffering the effects of the Condition. No matter how much she eats or drinks, she cannot gain nourishment until she possesses at least 1 point of Glamour. <b>This penalty applies to any changeling, not just the most powerful. </b>More powerful changelings begin to \u201cstarve\u201d at higher amounts of Glamour: those with Wyrd 6+ suffer from Glamour deprivation when their Glamour falls beneath their Wyrd rating. The most powerful changelings can sometimes seem greedy with their Glamour as a result, despite their vast stores of magical energy, always paranoid about falling into that desperation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank god catches exist...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-20-2016, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}